  "question": {
    "text": "A cylinder of fixed capacity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>44</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;litres contains helium gas at standard temperature and pressure. The amount of heat needed to raise the temperature of gas in the cylinder by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> will be (Given gas constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
