  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At STP&nbsp;volume occupied by one mole of a gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>. Therefore, number of moles are,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>44</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>.</p><p>The process is isochoric process as the volume of the cylinder remains fixed and&nbsp;helium is a monatomic gas. Therefore, amount of heat needed will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>Cv</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>20</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>498</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>",
